{"headword":"תָּמִים","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>adj. complete, sound</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 6:9\" href=\"/Genesis.6.9\">Gn 6:9</a> +; f. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִימָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 3:9\" href=\"/Leviticus.3.9\">Lv 3:9</a> +; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 36:4\" href=\"/Job.36.4\">Jb 36:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 37:16\" href=\"/Job.37.16\">37:16</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִימִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:25\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.25\">Ez 43:25</a> +; <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִימֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:15\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.15\">Lv 23:15</a>; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִימֵי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:1\" href=\"/Psalms.119.1\">ψ 119:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 11:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.11.20\">Pr 11:20</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>complete, whole, entire</em>, <a data-ref=\"Job 36:4\" href=\"/Job.36.4\">Jb 36:4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִים דֵעוֹת</span>, <a data-ref=\"Job 37:16\" href=\"/Job.37.16\">37:16</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>whole, sound, healthful</em>, of men <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:12\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.12\">Pr 1:12</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">חַיִּים</span>); vine <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 15:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.15.5\">Ez 15:5</a>; usually of sacrif. animals, P; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:5\" href=\"/Exodus.12.5\">Ex 12:5</a> + 40 times, so <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 43:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.43.22\">Ez 43:22</a> + 10 times"}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>complete, entire</em>, of time: day <a data-ref=\"Joshua 10:13\" href=\"/Joshua.10.13\">Jos 10:13</a>; year <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 25:30\" href=\"/Leviticus.25.30\">Lv 25:30</a>; sabbaths <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:15\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.15\">23:15</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"3."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>sound, wholesome, unimpaired, innocent, having integrity:</em> of God’s way <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:31\" href=\"/Psalms.18.31\">ψ 18:31</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:31\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.31\">2 S 22:31</a>; work <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 32:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.32.4\">Dt 32:4</a>; law <a data-ref=\"Psalms 19:8\" href=\"/Psalms.19.8\">ψ 19:8</a>; elsewhere of man <a data-ref=\"Genesis 6:9\" href=\"/Genesis.6.9\">Gn 6:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 17:1\" href=\"/Genesis.17.1\">17:1</a> (P; both ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אלהים</span> (<span dir=\"rtl\">לִפְנֵי</span>) <span dir=\"rtl\">הִתְהַלֵּךְ אֵת</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳ עם י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 18:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.18.13\">Dt 18:13</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:24\" href=\"/Psalms.18.24\">ψ 18:24</a>, c. ל in ‖ <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:24\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.24\">2 S 22:24</a>; often c. <span dir=\"rtl\">דֶרֶךְ</span> <em>way:</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">דֶּרֶךְ ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 101:2\" href=\"/Psalms.101.2\">ψ 101:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ת׳ בִּדְרָכֶ֫יךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 28:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.28.15\">Ez 28:15</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">תְּמִימֵי דָ֑רֶךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 11:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.11.20\">Pr 11:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:1\" href=\"/Psalms.119.1\">ψ 119:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיַּתֵּר ת׳ דרכו֯</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:23\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.23\">2 S 22:23</a> ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיִּתֵּן ת׳ דַּרְכִּי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:33\" href=\"/Psalms.18.33\">ψ 18:33</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הלך בדרך ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 101:6\" href=\"/Psalms.101.6\">101:6</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דֶּרֶךְ</span> om., <span dir=\"rtl\">הלך תמים</span>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:18\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.18\">Pr 28:18</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 15:2\" href=\"/Psalms.15.2\">ψ 15:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">לב ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 119:80\" href=\"/Psalms.119.80\">119:80</a>; = noun (late), man of <em>integrity</em> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 11:5\" href=\"/Proverbs.11.5\">Pr 11:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 12:4\" href=\"/Job.12.4\">Jb 12:4</a>; pl. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 2:21\" href=\"/Proverbs.2.21\">Pr 2:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 28:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.28.10\">28:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 37:18\" href=\"/Psalms.37.18\">ψ 37:18</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"4."},{"senses":[{"definition":"as neuter adj. = subst. <em>what is complete, entirely in accord with truth and fact:</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">דֹּבֵר ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Amos 5:10\" href=\"/Amos.5.10\">Am 5:10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אִם־בֶּאֱמֶת וּבְת׳ עֲשִׂיתֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 9:16\" href=\"/Judges.9.16\">Ju 9:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 9:19\" href=\"/Judges.9.19\">19</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עִבְדוּ י׳ בְּת׳ וּבֶאֱמֶת</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:14\" href=\"/Joshua.24.14\">Jos 24:14</a> (E); <em>integrity</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">גְּבַר ת׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 18:26\" href=\"/Psalms.18.26\">ψ 18:26</a> (cstr. Ges<sup>§ 93 s</sup>; ‖ <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 22:26\" href=\"/II_Samuel.22.26\">2 S 22:26</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גִּבּוֹר</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 84:12\" href=\"/Psalms.84.12\">84:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">הֹלְכִים בְּת׳</span>.—<a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:41\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.41\">1 S 14:41</a> v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, תֹּם²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_תֹּם²\">תֹּם</a> <strong>4</strong>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"5."}]},"rid":"BDB10885","strong_numbers":["8549"],"next_hw":"מְתֹם²","prev_hw":"תָּם","occurrences":"91","quotes":[],"GK":["9459"],"TWOT":["2522d"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}